  "result": "All 6 tests pass (4 existing plus the 2 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**What I changed** in `catalog/service.py`:\n\n- **find(substring)**: case-insensitive title match using casefold, returned in creation order as copies.\n- **export()**: returns the records as a JSON array in creation order.\n- **import_(dump)**: parses the dump, validates every record has exactly id, title, author as strings, and inserts them keeping their ids. It raises ValueError on malformed input or an id collision with existing records, and leaves the catalog untouched in that case. After a successful import it bumps the sequential id counter past any numeric imported id, so a later create() cannot hand out an id that was just imported. I verified this separately: importing ids 1 and 2 into a fresh catalog then creating a record yields id 3.\n\nNothing under tests/ was modified. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree.",
